{
  "brief_rationale": "The doctor met all responsibility-chain items (RC1-RC7), screening for danger symptoms, recognizing the urgency, addressing diuretic safety, identifying document gaps, providing concrete evaluation plans, defining emergency triggers, and maintaining safe boundaries. All five dimensions are at least good. High-order point HO4 (hidden state discovery) is complete through targeted workspace queries and integration of CKD/diabetic nephropathy history. HO1 (patient-state-sensitive communication) is complete with plain-language explanations adapted to the family's health literacy. No serious or minor in-chain error exists. Closure is valid_open with an active handoff to inpatient nephrology.",
