      "explanation": "The primary friction was low adherence/refusal, but the trajectory moved rapidly to emergency evaluation and inpatient admission before sustained refusal could become the main barrier. The doctor adapted to the family's initial hesitation about going to hospital by providing clear urgency rationale, but the family did not express ongoing refusal that required barrier repair work.",
